       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe, and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is twice the usual maximum.\n- The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n- Single doses usually don't exceed 850\u20131,000 mg.\n- A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
